1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,750
Majority Element — LeetCode 169

2
00:00:01,750 --> 00:00:04,600
Problem: return the value that appears more than n/2 times — the majority element, which is guaranteed to exist.

3
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:07,700
Example: in [2, 2, 1, 1, 2], 2 appears 3 times and 1 appears twice

4
00:00:07,700 --> 00:00:10,200
3 > 5/2, so the majority element is 2

5
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:15,000
Hint: a hash map costs O(n) space; instead, pair up different values and cancel them — the majority is more than half, so it always survives

6
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:20,100
Approach: Boyer-Moore voting — keep a candidate and a count; match → +1, mismatch → −1; when count hits 0, pick a new candidate

7
00:00:20,100 --> 00:00:24,650
Start: no candidate yet, count = 0

8
00:00:24,650 --> 00:00:26,930
count = 0 → nums[0] = 2 becomes the candidate

9
00:00:26,930 --> 00:00:29,140
2 matches the candidate → count + 1 = 1

10
00:00:29,140 --> 00:00:32,100
nums[1] = 2 matches → count + 1 = 2

11
00:00:32,100 --> 00:00:35,600
nums[2] = 1 differs → count − 1 = 1

12
00:00:35,600 --> 00:00:39,100
nums[3] = 1 differs → count − 1 = 0

13
00:00:39,100 --> 00:00:43,050
count = 0 → nums[4] = 2 becomes the candidate, count + 1 = 1

14
00:00:43,050 --> 00:00:45,990
Candidate = 2 → the majority element

15
00:00:45,990 --> 00:00:48,830
2 appears 3 of 5 — the majority

16
00:00:48,830 --> 00:00:51,580
Time O(n), space O(1)

17
